Arcane Index uses two licenses, applied by material type.

Software
========

Software source code is licensed under the MIT License. This includes build and
deployment configuration, application and component code, research scripts,
tests, and datasource query code. See LICENSE-MIT.

Research and documentation
==========================

Original datasets, research records, observations, findings, analysis, charts,
and written documentation are licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License (CC BY-SA 4.0). This includes
research/data, research/migrations, Markdown content in site/pages, and the
research material presented by the generated site. See LICENSE-CC-BY-SA-4.0.

Where a file contains both software and research or documentation, each part is
covered by the license applicable to that type of material.

Third-party material is not relicensed. It remains subject to the terms of its
respective owner or source.
